# Thrift Generated Layer (Layer B)

These trees are **Apache Thrift compiler output**. They are a separate standards layer from hand-written C++.

## Do

- Change API/types in `src/thrift/swcdb/Service.thrift` or `Broker.thrift`
- Regenerate via CMake (`thriftgen-${THRIFT_VERSION}` staging, then copy to consumer `gen-*`)
- Put business logic in hand-written wrappers: `thrift/broker/`, `thrift/client/`, `thrift/utils/`, or binding clients

## Do not

- Edit generated bodies for style, naming, formatting, or “clarity”
- Apply `.cursor/rules/cpp-conventions.mdc` (or other Layer A nits) to these files
- Add/remove project copyright headers or rewrite include guards inside generated trees
- Implement product behavior in `*_server.skeleton.cpp` or other generated skeletons

## Review

Use the **Layer B** checklist in `.cursor/rules/review-standards-clarity.mdc` (full report: `evals/STANDARDS_CLARITY_EVALUATION.md`).
